# The fixture filesystem clri's argument cases are pointed at -- task C4e.
#
# DELIBERATELY THE SMALLEST THING THAT IS A FILESYSTEM.  What these cases assert is the
# argument handling and the range check that v7 does not have, so nothing about the contents
# matters except that there is an i-list to be outside of.  The one that asserts what clri
# DOES is cmd_icheck_cleared, which needs icheck and dcheck to say what was done and so is
# registered in ../../icheck/test -- ../../icheck/test/run-icheck-cleared.sh says why it
# cannot live here.
#
# It is also its own fixture rather than a copy of anybody's for a reason that is not taste:
# cmd/clri is the first of the four added to the top-level CMakeLists.txt, so no other
# fixture target exists when this directory is configured.
#
# 20 blocks and a fixed timestamp: byte-reproducible, ../../df/test/fsimg.manifest's rule.
# The `source' path resolves against b6fsutil's working directory, this test's build
# directory.

default
owner 0
group 0
dirmode 0755
filemode 0644

file /f
source clriimg.d/small
